  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "The old UI was better than this in every way: it was intuitive, it looked good (or at least less \"corporate\" than this), and it didn't make me puke.\nIn all seriousness, though, the new UI update was... Not good in the slightest. Other than the new camera, that was cool. Then again, camera is PC only, so that also kind of doesn't exist for half of the users.\nThe wings system is annoying (I can't quite explain it, it's just not it, chief); the fact that now we only have 8 buttons in the main menu is beyond me, the size of each of the menus is very small, and that makes it less readable, the choice for the darker colours for the menu with the more opacity was REALLY not the right call, the fact that we have a lot of unlabeled smaller tabs is not exactly good, the banner at the top of most tabs is annoying, the rays that come out of the controllers are too slim (in fact, if you have shaky hands this new UI is a nightmare to go through), and the cursor is not here anymore. Sure, there's an ugly dot, but now it's less clear where it is, and it used to be something cool to look at during load times. That's gone now, and I just got to notice how long these load times actually are. Please bring back the old cursor, there was no plausible reason for any of these changes.\nThe menus are opaque now. This may not sound like a lot, but it's a choice that makes me disoriented; while before I could select things and still see the world behind the menu, that's not possible.\nThe default menu is too small, the tabs to open the wings are too small, the avatar icons in the wings are too small.\nThis new UI doesn't work. Please revert the changes.",
